  "conclusion": "The Scordelis-Lo failure of the flat-facet Shell4 is a rank deficiency of the element, not a property of faceting: with identical facets, load and diaphragms, replacing the one-point (sri) transverse-shear rule by assumed natural shear (mitc) removes 2 of the 3 spurious zero-energy mechanisms and moves the finest-mesh error from 49.4% to 0.75% (passes the 3% gate from 16x16 on: 2.34%). Equal-order full shear integration (the locking control) misses by 71.0% and still carries 1 spurious mechanism, confirming the shear block is the operative lever. The previously published attribution 'flat facets cannot capture curved-shell membrane-bending coupling' is therefore falsified as a statement about faceting."
